@startuml
title SmartPark - View Live Parking Availability (Issue #1)
autonumber

actor Student
participant "SmartPark React\ninterface" as React
participant "Backend application\nservice / API" as API
participant "Prisma ORM /\ndata-access layer" as Prisma
database PostgreSQL as DB
collections "Static CSV\n(prototype only)" as CSV

group Proposed database-backed flow - target architecture, not yet implemented
  Student -> React: Open parking availability
  React -> API: GET /api/parking/decks
  activate API
  API -> Prisma: Query active decks and latest occupancy reading per deck
  activate Prisma
  Prisma -> DB: SELECT decks and latest readings\nordered by observedAt DESC
  activate DB
  DB --> Prisma: Deck capacity and latest reading\n(count may be NULL)
  deactivate DB
  Prisma --> API: Decks with latest reading data
  deactivate Prisma
  API -> API: Derive available = capacity - occupied\nwhen count exists and is current
  API -> API: Mark missing, NULL, or stale readings unavailable
  API --> React: 200 JSON: decks, capacity,\navailable or unavailable, status, updatedAt
  deactivate API
  React --> Student: Display availability and freshness\nwithout manual page refresh

  loop Refresh every 30-60 seconds (Issue #1)
    React -> API: GET /api/parking/decks
    API -> Prisma: Read latest deck occupancy
    Prisma -> DB: SELECT latest readings
    DB --> Prisma: Current stored readings
    Prisma --> API: Decks and readings
    API --> React: Recalculated availability response
    React --> Student: Refresh displayed counts/status
  end
end

group Existing v2 prototype - CSV-based, no backend/database access
  Student -> React: Open availability page
  React -> CSV: fetch /data/parking.csv
  CSV --> React: Static demo deck rows
  React -> React: Parse CSV and calculate availability
  React --> Student: Display simulated availability
  loop Every 30 seconds while page is open
    React -> React: Randomly simulate occupancy changes
    React --> Student: Update browser-only counts
  end
  note over React, DB
    The current prototype does not call the API or Prisma,
    query PostgreSQL, or persist the simulated updates.
  end note
end
@enduml
